        'USA',
      ],
      timeline: [
        'Pre-1982: Folk game with home-made boards in Eastern USA.',
        '1982: Jax publishes Sequence as a commercial board game.',
        '2003: Quinto (Quinto Game Company) releases variant with scoring system.',
        'Present: Sequence remains popular; One-Eyed Jack name used for the traditional card-driven version.',
      ],
      evolution: 'From folk game with cut-and-glue boards to commercial Sequence. Double Series (Jouets Bo-Jeux) and Quinto offer alternative formats.',
      cultural: "Regional Eastern US favourite. The one-eyed vs two-eyed jack distinction (remove vs wild) is the game's defining mechanic.",
