        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Form one or more rows of five chips of your colour (or your team's) on the board. Rows can be horizontal, vertical, or diagonal.",
          gameplay: '1. **Turn**: Play one card face-up, place a chip on the matching unoccupied board space (or use jack power). 2. **Draw**: Replenish hand from stock. 3. **Two-eyed jack** (clubs, diamonds): Wildâ€”place your chip on any unoccupied space. 4. **One-eyed jack** (hearts, spades): Remove one opponent chip from the board. 5. **Win**: First player/team to complete a row of five chips wins.',
          keyRules: [
            'Play card â†’ place chip on matching space (or use jack).',
            'Two-eyed jack = place chip on any empty space.',
            'One-eyed jack = remove one opponent chip.',
            "Draw at end of turn. Play proceeds clockwise from dealer's left.",
            'Corner joker spaces: rules vary (free space, wild, or special).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Block opponents' rows. Use two-eyed jacks for hard-to-reach spaces. Save one-eyed jacks to break an opponent's four-in-a-row.",
          intermediate: 'Build multiple threats (two rows of four). Force opponents to block while you advance another line.',
          advanced: 'Partner coordination: one blocks, one builds. Track which cards are dead (both spaces occupied).',
          tips: [
            'Corners and edges can be valuableâ€”fewer directions for opponents to block.',
            'Dead cards (both spaces filled): some variants allow discard-and-draw; agree before play.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
